CHECK:BIT_MACRO: Prefer using the BIT macro
#162: FILE: arch/x86/include/uapi/asm/kvm_para.h:96:
+#define KVM_MIGRATION_READY		(1 << 0)

Defines like: 1 << <digit> could be BIT(digit).
The BIT() macro is defined via include/linux/bits.h::

  #define BIT(nr)         (1UL << (nr))

CHECK:UNNECESSARY_PARENTHESES: Unnecessary parentheses around 'vcpu->kvm'
#229: FILE: arch/x86/kvm/x86.c:3282:
+		if (data != !static_call(kvm_x86_has_encrypted_memory)(vcpu->kvm))

Parentheses are not required in the following cases:

  1. Function pointer uses::

      (foo->bar)();

    could be::

      foo->bar();

  2. Comparisons in if::

      if ((foo->bar) && (foo->baz))
      if ((foo == bar))

    could be::

      if (foo->bar && foo->baz)
      if (foo == bar)

  3. addressof/dereference single Lvalues::

      &(foo->bar)
      *(foo->bar)

    could be::

      &foo->bar
      *foo->bar

